    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Rf 4.3% (10y UST), beta ~0.75 (defensive waste oligopoly), ERP 5.0% -> CoE ~8.0%; pre-tax cost of debt ~4.6% (interest $574M FY25 on ~$13.5B avg debt), after-tax ~3.6%; D/V ~18% at market -> ~7.2%. Rounded up to 7.5% for leverage creep from debt-funded M&A and PFAS liability uncertainty. Same WACC in all three scenarios (risk charged once, via scenario paths and weights).",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP: operating lease cost (~$60M/yr, $226M liability) sits inside EBITDA as rent, so operating leases are NOT in net debt; finance leases ($293M) are inside total_debt (LongTermDebtAndCapitalLeaseObligations) and their principal is therefore NOT deducted from flows. One treatment each, never both.",
    "nci_treatment": "NCI immaterial ($1M on the June-2026 balance sheet); no adjustment.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component route (dcf-methods routing: US operating company -- a collection/transfer/landfill/recycling operator whose value is a free-cash-flow stream; not a REIT, bank, holdco or LIC). Adaptations file not needed (USD filer, USD quote, US GAAP leases, no NCI, SBC non-zero). FY0 is TTM to Jun-2026 so that year 1 (Jul-26..Jun-27) does not re-count H1-2026 cash already in the June balance sheet. REVENUE BASIS: uses us-gaap RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax (FY25 $16,591M, the reported net revenue that guidance is framed on); the Metrics.csv Revenue column carries the XBRL `Revenues` tag (FY25 $19,027M), which is GROSS of intercompany eliminations and overstates revenue ~15% -- every margin computed off that column is ~4pp too low. TTM components: net revenue 16,891; GAAP EBITDA (OI + D&A) 5,234 (31.0%); D&A 1,866 (11.0%); capex 1,889 (11.2%); OCF 4,542; asset-sale proceeds 12; reported FCF = OCF - capex + proceeds = 2,665 (levered, after ~$500M cash interest). Owner FCF (last_fcf) = 2,665 - 60 = 2,605. The engine's flows are UNLEVERED (EBIT x (1-t) + D&A - capex), so year-1 owner FCF (~$2.9B) sits above the levered TTM figure by roughly the after-tax interest bill; that is consistent, not a jump. EBITDA margin path is ex-SBC and NET of ~0.9pp of cash spent on landfill capping/closure/post-closure and environmental remediation (ARO settlements $70M FY25 plus remediation) that adjusted EBITDA excludes but OCF pays; the $2.8B of accrued closure/environmental liabilities is therefore charged in the flows and NOT put in the equity bridge. ACQUISITIONS: growth paths are ORGANIC (price minus volume) from year 2; tuck-in M&A ($1.43B FY25, $865M H1-26) is treated as NPV-neutral capital deployment, so neither the acquired revenue nor the spend is modelled. Deals closed by June 2026 are in net debt, and their rollover revenue is in year 1. Buybacks: active repurchaser ($870M FY25, $659M H1-26), so the flat count is funded with real cash. CASH TAX: FY25 cash taxes $206M (~8% of pre-tax) and H1-26 $79M are depressed by 100% bonus depreciation (deferred tax +$269M FY25) and purchased solar/renewable tax credits; book ETR ~17.5%. Modelled 15% ramping to 22% by year 8 -- not perpetuating the shelter, but not snapping to statutory either since bonus depreciation on a growing capex base defers tax persistently.",
